[9644]="70040B0F\n1\tClimb the foothills to the beacon at Nendath\tNendath can be found just south-east of Tadrent, along the foothills of the Emyn Ernil. You should hike up to Nendath and scout the valley for Corsair movements.\n2\tFight the intruders at Nendath (total: 6)\tFight the intruders at Nendath.\n3\tLook at Makham Mijann for signs of trouble\tFind a good spot on Nendath to look at the Corsair camp Makham Mijann.\n4\tTalk to Bruidis in Tadrent\tBruidis can be found back in Tadrent. Talk to Bruidis and tell her what you have seen. She will help you form a plan of action against the Corsairs at Makham Mijann.\n",
[9645]="7003A68D\n1\tTravel to Gapholt\tGapholt is south and west of Woodhurst, nestled on a cliff well above the Gap of Rohan. Gapholt is one of the few places still untouched by the war that surrounds it and has become a safe haven for Rohirrim refugees.\n2\tTalk to Toglos\030Talk to Hrothwaru\030Talk to Westan\tThe refugees in the line to get into Gapholt appear agitated by the long wait.\n3\tTalk to the bridge guard\tThere is a guard at the head of the line leading into Gapholt. You should talk to the guard to learn why everyone is waiting to enter the town.\n4\tTalk to Thane Nothmar\tThane Nothmar is near the bridge leading into Gapholt. You have been given permission to enter Gapholt and seek aid from Thane Nothmar.\n5\tThane Nothmar is near the bridge leading into Gapholt. Thane Nothmar has asked for help preparing Gapholt's defences for a possible attack.\t\n6\tTalk to Thane Nothmar\tThane Nothmar is near the bridge leading into Gapholt. With the defences prepared and supplies gathered for the journey, it is time to return to Thane Nothmar to make certain he fulfills his promise of aid.\n",
[9646]="7006C52B\n1\tDefeat Urâshi wasps (total: 12)\tYour mission is to travel to the Gorge of Woe and stop the hive-matron and her corrupted Urâshi wasps from spreading.\n2\tFind and defeat the hive-matron\tFind and defeat the hive-matron in the Gorge of Woe.\n",
[9647]="7005297E\n1\tDefeat vale-flies (total: 8)\030Defeat biting vale-gnat swarms (total: 8)\tVale-flies and biting vale-gnats can be found in the Beorning-lands. You should defeat vale-flies and biting vale-gnats.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated vale-flies and biting vale-gnats.\n",
[9648]="70048CA3\n1\tCatch Sneaky Tree-rats (quantity: see journal)\tSneaky tree-rats can be found in the limbs of trees in Agarnaith. You should catch some sneaky tree-rats for Viznak.\n2\tTalk to Viznak\tViznak can be found at his hideout. You should talk to Viznak.\n",
[9649]="70043E07\n1\tDefeat frenzied hendrevail (total: 12)\tHendrevail can be found on the eastern side of Osgiliath. You should defeat the pesky hendrevail.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have slaughtered many hendrevail in eastern Osgiliath.\n",
[9650]="7006AAF8\n1\tSearch for pest traps along the northern walls of Khabârkhad\tTilmakhím is to the south of Tâkhdar, but you know the traps are set along the northern walls of Khabârkhad. Journey there to search for pest traps.\n2\tLocate and remove traps (total: 4)\tTraps for rats can be found along the northern walls of Khabârkhad. Identify and remove the pest traps.\n3\tReturn to Hármelak\tHármelak is in Dâr Laja. You have found and removed the traps Hârmelak has said failed to capture pests and are a danger to her people. She will want to hear the good news.\n",
[9651]="7006B7E1\n1\tDefeat scather-flies at at Umûn Khab (total: 6)\030Defeat usan-kûni at Nirikal (total: 4)\tAkûshu has requested you slay some of the usan-kûni scorpions to the south at a place called Nirikal, and scather-flies in the bog near the river-bank at Umûn Khab.\n2\tTalk to Akûshu\tYou have slain many of the usan-kûni and scather-flies that posed a threat to the horses' safety. You should talk to Akûshu at Gha Nêkha, south of Eshadûr in Ambarûl.\n",
[9652]="70054665\n1\tDefeat insects in Cirith Ungol (total: 15)\tGladhir has asked you to defeat any insects you come across in Cirith Ungol.\n2\tTalk to Gladhir\tGladhir can be found in Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol. You should talk to Gladhir.\n",
[9653]="7005A6A1\n1\tDefeat the Orc who has Oda's tools\tThe Orc who stole Oda's tools retreated to Târ-kútoz, the Orc camp to the west of Ashmargathâl. However, Oda does not know which Orc is responsible. You should defeat Orcs to see which one has her tools.\n2\tTalk to Oda\tYou have found Oda's tools. You should return them to her at Ashmargathâl.\n",
[9654]="70071CC8\n1\tRecover Jûshal's ancient heirloom\tJûshal has requested your aid in retrieving a family heirloom of his. Locals brigands stole it, and he believes they have taken it back to their camp, the Hold of Jalkhíla. The Hold of Jalkhíla can be found north of Sen Chatâk.\n2\tReturn to Jûshal in Sen Chatâk\tReturn to Jûshal in Sen Chatâk.\n",
[9655]="7002F933\n1\tTalk to Athelward's cook, Cetelgat, about the poison\tCetelgat can be found working in Reeve Athelward's kitchen, just west of the Cliving Mead Hall. Walnoth has asked you to speak with Cetelgat, the Reeve's cook, about the phial he found in the kitchen.\n2\tExamine the phial of strange liquid\tThe phial can be found near Cetelgat in the Reeve's kitchen. Cetelgat has given you information regarding the phial. The phial may be inspected further to determine its contents.\n3\tReturn to Walnoth to discuss what you have learned\tWalnoth waits at the centre of the city of Cliving, by the water fountain. The phial has been inspected, and Walnoth awaits your return with the information.\n4\tEnter Malbéort's house to speak with him\tMalbéort's residence can be found in the back of the market area in Cliving, west of the fountain. Walnoth has asked you to visit Malbéort at his residence and to inquire as to who may have been in possession of the phial of poison.\n5\tInspect Malbéort carefully\tMalbéort's residence can be found in the back of the market area in Cliving, west of the fountain. Malbéort lies on the floor, wounded and unmoving. It would be wise to investigate further.\n6\tSearch for a murder-weapon within Malbéort's home\tMalbéort's residence can be found in the back of the market area in Cliving, west of the fountain. Malbéort's home can be searched for evidence of a murder-weapon.\n7\tReturn to Walnoth with the dagger\tWalnoth awaits your return at the centre of Cliving, by the fountain. Walnoth needs to be informed of what you have discovered at Malbéort's home.\n",
[9656]="7004E934\n1\tTalk to Radagast\tYou should return to Radagast, located at the highest point of Thornholt.\n2\tCollect Ungoladan-poison (total: 4)\030Collect fresh water (quantity: see journal)\030Collect animal livers (total: 5)\030Collect mushrooms (total: 5)\tAll the items can be found in and around the Thornholt woods. You should collect the ingredients Radagast requires for the potion of protection against the Ungoladan-poison: poison from discarded Ungoladan weapons, fresh water, livers of animals sickened from the poison, and the mushrooms common to Thornholt.\n3\tBring the ingredients to Radagast\tYou should return to Radagast in Thornholt with all the ingredients you have collected.\n4\tMix ingredients in mortar and pestle\tYou should place all the ingredients in the nearby mortar and pestle for Radagast, in Thornholt woods.\n5\tBring the concoction to Radagast\tRadagast can be found in the Thornholt woods. You should return to Radagast with the mixed concoction.\n6\tTalk to Vaskorn in Skoghús\tYou should return to Vaskorn in Skoghús, in the Thornholt woods, and tell him of Radagast's potion.\n7\tTalk to Threkmóth\tYou should go to Threkmóth in Skoghús, in the Thornholt woods, and find out where Vaskorn is.\n",
[9657]="70057191\n1\tPick wild berries (total: 10)\tWild berries can be found in the Beorninglands. You should pick some wild berries.\n2\tGive the wild berries to Gírta at the Beorninghús\tGírta can be found at the Beorninghús. You should give the wild berries to Gírta.\n",
[9658]="700529D3\n1\tRemove meat scraps (total: 5)\030Tend to trampled plants (total: 3)\030Remove broken wood (total: 7)\030Remove abandoned weapons (total: 5)\tThe goblins that came through Ainhard's homestead left a mess in their wake. You should clean up meat scraps, abandoned weapons, trampled plants, and broken wood.\n2\tTalk to Langhár\tLanghár can be summoned to your side with Langhár's summoning horn. You should talk to Langhár.\n",
[9659]="70008B8C\n1\tBring the crate of pick-axes to Wegeir\tWegeir is somewhere within Thorin's Hall. Ormulf Worm-hunter has been impressed by your selflessness and asked you to deliver a crate of pick-axes to Wegeir, who can give to you your reward.\n",
[9660]="700078EA\n1\tThe south-easternmost stump in the stump-field -- the one closest to Staddle Falls -- was once the Hanging Tree. After reading through the ledger you recovered for him, Mason Thorne was able to point you to the location of the Hanging Tree.\t\n2\tBring Pickthorn's boots to Ted Pickthorn\tTed Pickthorn is on the east side of Combe. Following Thorne's instructions, you found the stump of the Hanging Tree. You dug up something buried beneath the stump, but it is not what Ted Pickthorn had led you to believe. His father's treasure appears to be a pair of old boots.\n",
[9661]="70000D15\n1\tPick up the pie from the table\tGerd Whitfoot is at The Green Dragon Inn in Bywater. Holly Hornblower has asked you to deliver a pie to Gerd Whitfoot at The Green Dragon in Bywater. She warned you to not allow any hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, or they will come by pestering her for a slice, and she has no time for that. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Holly Hornblower\tHolly Hornblower can be found north of Hobbiton's main square, behind The Ivy Bush. You should return to Holly Hornblower and let her know that the pie has been delivered.\n",
[9662]="7003FC34\n1\tCollect arrows from the fields outside Morlad (total: 10)\tArrows can be found littering the ground and the corpses of slain Orcs outside Morlad. Uidor has asked you to retrieve arrows so that the guards of Morlad might conserve their dwindling resources.\n2\tDeliver the recovered arrows to Uidor\tUidor can be found near the entrance to Morlad in north-west Blackroot Vale. You have recovered many arrows from the fields of Blackroot Vale and should now return them to Uidor.\n",
[9663]="70032B97\n1\tSearch piles of skulls (total: 8)\tPiles of skulls can be found in the Orc encampment at Mudmul-charâf. You should search the piles of skulls to see what the Orcs have been up to.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have searched many of the skull-piles in Mudmul-charâf and learned that the Orcs of this area were likely raiding ancient tombs in Zelem-melek for keepsakes.\n",
[9664]="7003FF7D\n1\tDefeat looters (total: 6)\tThe looters must be stopped.\n",
})
